    "created_at": "2016-12-20T06:29:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-20T06:30:57Z",
    "body": "I think having it on `console` just follows the precedent of `profile`, `profileEnd`, and `timeStamp`. It just so happens that `console` is the namespace where new Web APIs have gone that programmatically interact with browser developer tools. It is not surprising that these are the ones that Node doesn't include on their `console` object which is more geared toward some kind of real console.\r\n\r\n`console.timeStamp` could be considered similar / identical to [`performance.mark`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Performance/mark). Maybe there could be a new place for these other commands instead of `console`? Moving would be inconvenient but not impossible.\r\n\r\nThat said, I don't think there is much to spec here other than the interface.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
